// The control: a file that does NOT declare the leak-verdict pragma still
// runs (and still counts) when the leak verdict is staged off — the skip
// applies only to the files that declare it. (Written without the pragma's
// literal spelling: the runner detects it with a text scan of the first 50
// lines, comments included, so naming it here would skip this file too.)
{ assert } :: import("std/assert");

test("plain test still runs under the ratchet", {
  assert(true, "ok");
});
